<!--
  Slide 04 — Inflection Date & Methodology
  Type: content-slide
  Required tokens (substituted by render_deck.py from
  acceleration/data/inflection.json and acceleration/data/metrics.json):
    {{INFLECTION_DATE}}    Detected inflection date (ISO YYYY-MM-DD).
                           Sourced from inflection.json:"date".
    {{INFLECTION_METHOD}}  Detection method label, e.g., "convergent_evidence".
                           Sourced from inflection.json:"method". One of
                           "convergent_evidence" | "single_signal" |
                           "earliest_ai_trailer" — see AAP §0.3.1.2 decision flow.
    {{BASELINE_START}}     First commit date in the repository (ISO).
                           Sourced from metrics.json:"environment.first_commit_date".
                           Used as the Gantt start of the Baseline section.
    {{BASELINE_END}}       Day before inflection (ISO).
                           Sourced from inflection.json:"baseline_end".
                           Used as the Gantt end of the Baseline section.
    {{RAMPUP_END}}         End of Ramp-Up phase (ISO) = inflection + 84 days.
                           Sourced from inflection.json:"rampup_end".
                           Per AAP §0.8.4 — "Ramp-Up is exactly six windows
                           (84 days, the largest multiple of 14 ≤ 90)".
    {{STEADY_END}}         Latest commit date in the analysis window (ISO).
                           Sourced from metrics.json:"environment.last_commit_date".
                           Used as the Gantt end of the Steady State section.
  Required non-text visual: Mermaid timeline diagram in <pre class="mermaid">…</pre>
  (satisfies Rule 5 content-slide visual requirement). Additional visual: a
  Lucide "git-branch" icon next to the detected-date line.

  Diagram type — historical note: a previous revision of this template used
  Mermaid ``gantt`` with ``tickInterval 1year`` to show the temporal phases
  as a horizontal bar chart against a year-marked axis. Mermaid 11.15.0 emits
  one tick per quarter regardless of ``tickInterval`` for multi-year gantt
  charts (verified with an isolated repro at this version), which produced
  ~17 overlapping year labels that smeared into an unreadable strip at the
  axis. The ``timeline`` chart type (introduced in Mermaid 8.14) has no
  axis density problem because each labeled milestone is a discrete box;
  the chart auto-arranges them with even spacing and zero overlap. We trade
  the proportional-span visualization for a discrete-milestone visualization
  in exchange for guaranteed readability — the diagram-legend below the
  chart restores the proportional intuition in prose.

  Authority:
    - AAP §0.4.1 (file inventory enumerates slide_04_inflection.html.tmpl).
    - AAP §0.3.1.2 (Inflection Detection Decision Flow — this slide is the
      executive-readable summary of that algorithm; the report's Methodology
      section carries the full prose, satisfying Rule 4 — Internal Consistency).
    - AAP §0.7.1 Rule 4 (Visual Architecture Documentation — Mermaid is the
      sole diagramming language; every diagram MUST have a descriptive title;
      satisfied by the gantt `title` line).
    - AAP §0.7.1 Rule 5 (Executive Presentation — content-slide constraints:
      max 4 bullets, ≤40 body words, ≥1 non-text visual, zero emoji, no
      fenced code blocks — the only <pre> tag here is class="mermaid").
    - AAP §0.8.4 (Temporal Phases — Baseline / Ramp-Up (first 84 days) /
      Steady State (window seven onward)). The three gantt sections mirror
      these three phases by name and ordering.
    - theme.css §Phase 10 (Mermaid container styling — padding, border,
      min-height for the rendering window).
    - theme.css §Phase 11 (Lucide icon defaults — color: var(--brand-primary),
      width/height: 32px on top-level usage).

  Rendering notes:
    - This template is consumed by render_deck.py, which substitutes the six
      tokens above from inflection.json + metrics.json and writes the result
      into acceleration/executive-presentation.html.
    - Mermaid runtime: the deck initializes Mermaid 11.15.0 with
      startOnLoad:false, theme:'base', and a timeline-friendly default
      configuration. ``mermaid.run()`` is invoked on Reveal "ready" and
      "slidechanged" events, so the <pre class="mermaid"> block is
      transformed to inline <svg> at slide-enter time. The Blitzy palette
      is applied via the themeVariables passed by the parent HTML —
      timeline sections inherit ``primaryColor`` (Baseline & Steady State
      bars use ``#5B39F3``) and ``secondaryColor`` (alternating sections
      use ``#94FAD5``).
    - Lucide runtime: lucide.createIcons() is called on the same events,
      replacing the <i data-lucide="git-branch"> tag with the corresponding
      <svg data-lucide="git-branch"> element; theme.css §Phase 11 selectors
      target both forms.
    - Mermaid timeline task syntax: ``<event label> : <event description>``
      under a ``section <name>`` heading. Each event renders as a labeled
      box with the description attached beneath. The three sections
      (Baseline, Ramp-Up, Steady State) mirror AAP §0.8.4 verbatim and
      appear in chronological order so the visual narrative reads
      left-to-right.
    - Token-substituted dates conform to ISO YYYY-MM-DD and appear as the
      event label, so the milestone date is the most prominent text on
      each box.
    - Indentation inside <pre class="mermaid"> is preserved; the ``timeline``
      directive must remain at column 0 of its own line within the <pre>,
      with ``section`` declarations indented by four spaces and event lines
      indented by eight spaces, matching the Mermaid 11.15.0 timeline
      parser's expected whitespace.
    - The timeline body uses ASCII-only characters. Mermaid 11.15.0's
      timeline renderer mis-handles certain UTF-8 multi-byte sequences
      (notably U+00B7 MIDDLE DOT) when embedded inside event descriptions,
      rendering them as mojibake in the output SVG. We use ``-`` and
      plain words instead. UTF-8 characters in HTML text outside the
      ``<pre class="mermaid">`` block render correctly because they are
      processed by the browser rather than by Mermaid.

  Tone discipline (AAP §0.7.2.2 Rule 2 — Factual-Neutral): the section
  labels are technical terms ("Pre-AI Tool", "First 84 days", "90+ days")
  and the forbidden subjective-qualifier list in the Boundaries directive
  does not appear in the visible slide body. "Detected:" and "Method:"
  are neutral status descriptors. The method label "convergent_evidence"
  is the technical name of the algorithm branch per AAP §0.3.1.2, not
  editorial framing.

  Body word count outside <pre> (after token substitution):
    Eyebrow "Methodology" (1) + Heading "Inflection Date & Temporal
    Phases" (5) + Paragraph "Detected: <date> · Method: <method>" (4)
    ≈ 10 words, well under the Rule 5 cap of 40.

  Verification (verify_report.py asserts):
    - Exactly one top-level <section> with class="content-slide".
    - Zero emoji codepoints.
    - The only <pre> tag is class="mermaid" (no fenced code blocks).
    - At least one non-text visual (Mermaid block + Lucide icon).
    - Exactly one <p class="diagram-legend"> element appears after the
      Mermaid block, satisfying Rule 4 (Visual Architecture Documentation —
      every diagram MUST have a descriptive title AND an explanatory
      legend).
    - All six tokens {{INFLECTION_DATE}}, {{INFLECTION_METHOD}},
      {{BASELINE_START}}, {{BASELINE_END}}, {{RAMPUP_END}},
      {{STEADY_END}} appear unsubstituted in the template source and are
      substituted to non-empty strings in the rendered HTML.
-->
<section class="content-slide">
  <span class="eyebrow">Methodology</span>
  <h3>Inflection Date &amp; Temporal Phases</h3>
  <p><i data-lucide="git-branch" aria-hidden="true"></i> Detected: <strong>{{INFLECTION_DATE}}</strong> · Method: {{INFLECTION_METHOD}}</p>
  <pre class="mermaid">
timeline
    title Temporal Phases (Monday-aligned 2-week windows)
    section Baseline
        {{BASELINE_START}} : Pre-AI baseline begins
        {{BASELINE_END}} : 95 windows recorded
    section Ramp-Up (84 days)
        {{INFLECTION_DATE}} : Inflection - AI tool introduced
        {{RAMPUP_END}} : End of Ramp-Up phase
    section Steady State
        {{STEADY_END}} : Latest commit (window 7 onward)
  </pre>
  <p class="diagram-legend"><i data-lucide="info" aria-hidden="true"></i> Baseline = repository activity before the inflection date (≈{{BASELINE_START}} → {{BASELINE_END}}). Ramp-Up = the first 84 days after (six 2-week windows). Steady State = window seven onward, through {{STEADY_END}}.</p>
</section>
